2026-05-28 11:55:00,542 | DEBUG | anthropic._base_client | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1e302403-64e5-418f-9355-9a5cc33ae2d3', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 8192, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Requirement (natural language):\nImplement a producer-consumer system with three components:\n\n  1. A bounded FIFO queue of capacity 3. Items are positive integers in\n     1..10. Enqueue is rejected when the queue is full; dequeue is rejected\n     when the queue is empty.\n  2. A producer that generates items 1..3 in order and enqueues them.\n  3. A consumer that dequeues items and tracks the running sum.\n\nSafety properties:\n  - The queue length is always in 0..3.\n  - No item is ever lost: every item produced is eventually consumed in\n    FIFO order (i.e. consumer.received is a prefix of producer.generated).\n  - The producer never produces beyond item 3.\n\nApproved decomposition plan:\nParent: ProducerConsumerSystem\nParent role: Composes the bounded FIFO queue with a producer and consumer, wiring producer enqueues and consumer dequeues through the queue and asserting FIFO no-loss and bounded-length safety.\n\nChild modules:\n  - BoundedQueue: A bounded FIFO buffer of capacity 3 holding integers in 1..10, with enqueue rejected on full and dequeue rejected on empty.\n      state_variables: buffer\n      actions: Enqueue, Dequeue\n      invariant_sketch: Buffer length is always between 0 and 3 and every element is an integer in 1..10.\n  - Producer: Generates the items 1, 2, 3 in order and offers them to the queue, recording what has been generated.\n      state_variables: generated, nextItem\n      actions: Produce\n      invariant_sketch: The generated sequence is a prefix of <<1,2,3>> and nextItem never exceeds 4.\n  - Consumer: Dequeues items from the queue, appends them to a received log, and maintains a running sum.\n      state_variables: received, runningSum\n      actions: Consume\n      invariant_sketch: runningSum equals the sum of received and received only grows by appending dequeued items.\n\nExpand this plan into a ModuleBundle. For each child, emit both <Name>_Abs (pure TLA+) and <Name>_Impl (PlusCal-bearing TLA+). Emit a parent module that INSTANCEs each impl and defines its own composed Inv and Property. Pin small finite CONSTANTS so TLC can model-check exhaustively. Emit one call to propose_module_bundle.'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AadZBHWy1Yk3upFipDK9eL', 'name': 'propose_module_bundle', 'input': {'slug': 'producer_consumer_system', 'parent': {'name': 'ProducerConsumerSystem', 'invariant_name': 'Inv', 'property_name': 'Property', 'tla_source': '---- MODULE ProducerConsumerSystem ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANTS Capacity, MaxItem\n\nVARIABLES buffer, generated, nextItem, received, runningSum,\n          pcQ, pcP, pcC\n\nQ == INSTANCE BoundedQueue_Impl WITH buffer <- buffer, pc <- pcQ\nP == INSTANCE Producer_Impl     WITH generated <- generated, nextItem <- nextItem, pc <- pcP\nC == INSTANCE Consumer_Impl     WITH received <- received, runningSum <- runningSum, pc <- pcC\n\nvars == << buffer, generated, nextItem, received, runningSum, pcQ, pcP, pcC >>\n\nInit == Q!Init /\\ P!Init /\\ C!Init\nNext == (Q!Next /\\ UNCHANGED << generated, nextItem, received, runningSum, pcP, pcC >>)\n     \\/ (P!Next /\\ UNCHANGED << buffer, received, runningSum, pcQ, pcC >>)\n     \\/ (C!Next /\\ UNCHANGED << buffer, generated, nextItem, pcP, pcQ >>)\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nIsPrefix(s, t) == Len(s) <= Len(t) /\\ (\\A i \\in 1..Len(s) : s[i] = t[i])\n\nInv == /\\ Q!Inv\n       /\\ P!Inv\n       /\\ C!Inv\n       /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n       /\\ IsPrefix(received, generated)\n       /\\ nextItem \\in 1..(MaxItem+1)\n\nProperty == /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n            /\\ IsPrefix(received, generated)\n            /\\ nextItem <= MaxItem + 1\n====\n', 'constants': {'values': {'Capacity': [3], 'MaxItem': [3]}}}, 'modules': [{'name': 'BoundedQueue', 'role': 'abs', 'tla_source': "---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Abs ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT Capacity\n\nVARIABLE queue\n\nvars == << queue >>\n\nInit == queue = << >>\n\nEnqueue(v) == /\\ Len(queue) < Capacity\n              /\\ v \\in 1..10\n              /\\ queue' = Append(queue, v)\n\nDequeue == /\\ Len(queue) > 0\n           /\\ queue' = Tail(queue)\n\nNext == (\\E v \\in 1..10 : Enqueue(v)) \\/ Dequeue\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv == /\\ Len(queue) \\in 0..Capacity\n       /\\ \\A i \\in 1..Len(queue) : queue[i] \\in 1..10\n\nProperty == Len(queue) \\in 0..Capacity\n====\n", 'constants': {'values': {'Capacity': [3]}}}, {'name': 'BoundedQueue', 'role': 'impl', 'tla_source': '---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT Capacity\n\n(* --algorithm BoundedQueue\nvariables buffer = << >>;\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while TRUE do\n      either\n        await Len(buffer) < Capacity;\n        with v \\in 1..10 do\n          buffer := Append(buffer, v);\n        end with;\n      or\n        await Len(buffer) > 0;\n        buffer := Tail(buffer);\n      end either;\n    end while;\n  Finish:\n    skip;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nInv == /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n       /\\ \\A i \\in 1..Len(buffer) : buffer[i] \\in 1..10\n       /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Finish", "Done"}\n\nProperty == Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n====\n', 'pluscal_source': '---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT Capacity\n\n(* --algorithm BoundedQueue\nvariables buffer = << >>;\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while TRUE do\n      either\n        await Len(buffer) < Capacity;\n        with v \\in 1..10 do\n          buffer := Append(buffer, v);\n        end with;\n      or\n        await Len(buffer) > 0;\n        buffer :