t. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Producer :: consec: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Producer :: property: ERROR\n    note: TLC could not enumerate states from the spec/invariant: identifier `generated` is undefined or unbounded. This usually means `Inv` (used as the initial predicate for the consec/property checks) does not bound a variable via explicit set membership.\nComputing initial states...\nError: In evaluation, the identifier generated is either undefined or not an operator.\nline 57, col 15 to line 57, col 23 of module Producer_Impl\nError: The error occurred when TLC was evaluating the nested\nexpressions at the following positions:\n0. Line 5, column 10 to line 5, column 12 in Prop_Producer_Impl\n1. Line 56, column 8 to line 59, column 43 in Producer_Impl\n2. Line 56, column 11 to line 56, column 37 in Producer_Impl\n3. Line 57, column 11 to line 57, column 39 in Producer_Impl\n4. Line 57, column 11 to line 57, column 24 in Producer_Impl\n- module Consumer :: init: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Consumer :: consec: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Consumer :: property: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\nFirst error line: In computing initial states, the right side of \\IN is not enumerable.\n- refinement obligation: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n\nLast bundle slug: producer_consumer_system\nParent module: ProducerConsumerSystem\nModules: BoundedQueue(abs), BoundedQueue(impl), Producer(abs), Producer(impl), Consumer(abs), Consumer(impl)\nRevise the failing module(s) and/or abstraction map(s). Return one call to repair_module_bundle with the FULL revised bundle."}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01R7xSQ5zu3RPQsytn4Ske4p', 'name': 'repair_module_bundle', 'input': {'reasoning': "The Inv used for consec/property checks needs to explicitly bound variables via set-membership (Inv is used as the init predicate). I'm strengthening each impl's Inv to include explicit type bounds like `buffer \\in Seq(1..10)` and `generated \\in Seq(1..MaxItem)`, `received \\in Seq(1..10)`, `runningSum \\in 0..(MaxItem*(MaxItem+1)/2)` (bounded), and pc \\in {...}. Also the Consumer_Abs Init/Next used `\\E v \\in 1..10` which is fine, but Consumer_Impl had unbounded Nat — replace with explicit bounded set. Also limit MaxItem and avoid infinite Consumer loop by stopping when nothing to consume (but to keep it simple in standalone Impl checking, bound runningSum and received length so enumeration is finite). Easiest: make Consumer Impl loop bounded by a constant, but the standalone module would run forever. The TLC error for Consumer init says \\IN right side not enumerable — that's from `\\E v \\in 1..10` for `with v`... actually `with v \\in 1..10` is fine. The init error is probably from `runningSum \\in Nat` in the Inv being used as init constraint. Replace Nat with a finite bound. Also for BoundedQueue Inv, replace bare `Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity` with explicit `buffer \\in UNION { [1..n -> 1..10] : n \\in 0..Capacity }` to make it enumerable. Simpler approach: use bounded Seq with explicit set.", 'targeted_failure': 'multiple/init+consec — Inv not enumerable', 'slug': 'producer_consumer_system', 'parent': {'name': 'ProducerConsumerSystem', 'invariant_name': 'Inv', 'property_name': 'Property', 'tla_source': '---- MODULE ProducerConsumerSystem ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANTS Capacity, MaxItem\n\nVARIABLES buffer, generated, nextItem, received, runningSum,\n          pcQ, pcP, pcC\n\nQ == INSTANCE BoundedQueue_Impl WITH buffer <- buffer, pc <- pcQ\nP == INSTANCE Producer_Impl     WITH generated <- generated, nextItem <- nextItem, pc <- pcP\nC == INSTANCE Consumer_Impl     WITH received <- received, runningSum <- runningSum, pc <- pcC\n\nvars == << buffer, generated, nextItem, received, runningSum, pcQ, pcP, pcC >>\n\nInit == Q!Init /\\ P!Init /\\ C!Init\nNext == (Q!Next /\\ UNCHANGED << generated, nextItem, received, runningSum, pcP, pcC >>)\n     \\/ (P!Next /\\ UNCHANGED << buffer, received, runningSum, pcQ, pcC >>)\n     \\/ (C!Next /\\ UNCHANGED << buffer, generated, nextItem, pcP, pcQ >>)\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nIsPrefix(s, t) == Len(s) <= Len(t) /\\ (\\A i \\in 1..Len(s) : s[i] = t[i])\n\nInv == /\\ Q!Inv\n       /\\ P!Inv\n       /\\ C!Inv\n       /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n       /\\ IsPrefix(received, generated)\n       /\\ nextItem \\in 1..(MaxItem+1)\n\nProperty == /\\ Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n            /\\ IsPrefix(received, generated)\n            /\\ nextItem <= MaxItem + 1\n====\n', 'constants': {'values': {'Capacity': [3], 'MaxItem': [3]}}}, 'modules': [{'name': 'BoundedQueue', 'role': 'abs', 'tla_source': "---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Abs ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT Capacity\n\nVARIABLE queue\n\nvars == << queue >>\n\nBoundedSeqs == UNION { [1..n -> 1..10] : n \\in 0..Capacity }\n\nInit == queue = << >>\n\nEnqueue(v) == /\\ Len(queue) < Capacity\n              /\\ v \\in 1..10\n              /\\ queue' = Append(queue, v)\n\nDequeue == /\\ Len(queue) > 0\n           /\\ queue' = Tail(queue)\n\nNext == (\\E v \\in 1..10 : Enqueue(v)) \\/ Dequeue\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv == queue \\in BoundedSeqs\n\nProperty == Len(queue) \\in 0..Capacity\n====\n", 'constants': {'values': {'Capacity': [3]}}}, {'name': 'BoundedQueue', 'role': 'impl', 'tla_source': '---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT Capacity\n\n(* --algorithm BoundedQueue\nvariables buffer = << >>;\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while TRUE do\n      either\n        await Len(buffer) < Capacity;\n        with v \\in 1..10 do\n          buffer := Append(buffer, v);\n        end with;\n      or\n        await Len(buffer) > 0;\n        buffer := Tail(buffer);\n      end either;\n    end while;\n  Finish:\n    skip;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nBoundedSeqs == UNION { [1..n -> 1..10] : n \\in 0..Capacity }\n\nInv == /\\ buffer \\in BoundedSeqs\n       /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Finish", "Done"}\n\nProperty == Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n====\n', 'pluscal_source': '---- MODULE BoundedQueue_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT Capacity\n\n(* --algorithm BoundedQueue\nvariables buffer = << >>;\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while TRUE do\n      either\n        await Len(buffer) < Capacity;\n        with v \\in 1..10 do\n          buffer := Append(buffer, v);\n        end with;\n      or\n        await Len(buffer) > 0;\n        buffer := Tail(buffer);\n      end either;\n    end while;\n  Finish:\n    skip;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nBoundedSeqs == UNION { [1..n -> 1..10] : n \\in 0..Capacity }\n\nInv == /\\ buffer \\in BoundedSeqs\n       /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Finish", "Done"}\n\nProperty == Len(buffer) \\in 0..Capacity\n====\n', 'abstraction_map': {'queue': 'buffer'}, 'constants': {'values': {'Capacity': [3]}}}, {'name': 'Producer', 'role': 'abs', 'tla_source': "---- MODULE Producer_Abs ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT MaxItem\n\nVARIABLES generated, nextItem\n\nvars == << generated, nextItem >>\n\nFullSeq == [ i \\in 1..MaxItem |-> i ]\n\nPrefixSeqs == { [ i \\in 1..n |-> i ] : n \\in 0..MaxItem }\n\nInit == /\\ generated = << >>\n        /\\ nextItem = 1\n\nProduce == /\\ nextItem <= MaxItem\n           /\\ generated' = Append(generated, nextItem)\n           /\\ nextItem' = nextItem + 1\n\nNext == Produce\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv == /\\ nextItem \\in 1..(MaxItem+1)\n       /\\ generated \\in PrefixSeqs\n       /\\ Len(generated) = nextItem - 1\n\nProperty == nextItem <= MaxItem + 1\n====\n", 'constants': {'values': {'MaxItem': [3]}}}, {'name': 'Producer', 'role': 'impl', 'tla_source': '---- MODULE Producer_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT MaxItem\n\n(* --algorithm Producer\nvariables generated = << >>, nextItem = 1;\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while nextItem <= MaxItem do\n      generated := Append(generated, nextItem);\n      nextItem := nextItem + 1;\n    end while;\n  Finish:\n    skip;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nFullSeq == [ i \\in 1..MaxItem |-> i ]\n\nPrefixSeqs == { [ i \\in 1..n |-> i ] : n \\in 0..MaxItem }\n\nInv == /\\ nextItem \\in 1..(MaxItem+1)\n       /\\ generated \\in PrefixSeqs\n       /\\ Len(generated) = nextItem - 1\n       /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Finish", "Done"}\n\nProperty == nextItem <= MaxItem + 1\n====\n', 'pluscal_source': '---- MODULE Producer_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT MaxItem\n\n(* --algorithm Producer\nvariables generated = << >>, nextItem = 1;\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while nextItem <= MaxItem do\n      generated := Append(generated, nextItem);\n      nextItem := nextItem + 1;\n    end while;\n  Finish:\n    skip;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nFullSeq == [ i \\in 1..MaxItem |-> i ]\n\nPrefixSeqs == { [ i \\in 1..n |-> i ] : n \\in 0..MaxItem }\n\nInv == /\\ nextItem \\in 1..(MaxItem+1)\n       /\\ generated \\in PrefixSeqs\n       /\\ Len(generated) = nextItem - 1\n       /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Finish", "Done"}\n\nProperty == nextItem <= MaxItem + 1\n====\n', 'abstraction_map': {'generated': 'generated', 'nextItem': 'nextItem'}, 'constants': {'values': {'MaxItem': [3]}}}, {'name': 'Consumer', 'role': 'abs', 'tla_source': "---- MODULE Consumer_Abs ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT MaxLen\n\nVARIABLES received, runningSum\n\nvars == << received, runningSum >>\n\nBoundedReceived == UNION { [1..n -> 1..10] : n \\in 0..MaxLen }\n\nInit == /\\ received = << >>\n        /\\ runningSum = 0\n\nConsume(v) == /\\ v \\in 1..10\n              /\\ Len(received) < MaxLen\n              /\\ received' = Append(received, v)\n              /\\ runningSum' = runningSum + v\n\nNext == \\E v \\in 1..10 : Consume(v)\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv == /\\ received \\in BoundedReceived\n       /\\ runningSum \\in 0..(MaxLen*10)\n\nProperty == runningSum \\in 0..(MaxLen*10)\n====\n", 'constants': {'values': {'MaxLen': [3]}}}, {'name': 'Consumer', 'role': 'impl', 'tla_source': '---- MODULE Consumer_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT MaxLen\n\n(* --algorithm Consumer\nvariables received = << >>, runningSum = 0;\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while Len(received) < MaxLen do\n      with v \\in 1..10 do\n        received := Append(received, v);\n        runningSum := runningSum + v;\n      end with;\n    end while;\n  Finish:\n    skip;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nBoundedReceived == UNION { [1..n -> 1..10] : n \\in 0..MaxLen }\n\nInv == /\\ received \\in BoundedReceived\n       /\\ runningSum \\in 0..(MaxLen*10)\n       /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Finish", "Done"}\n\nProperty == runningSum \\in 0..(MaxLen*10)\n====\n', 'pluscal_source': '---- MODULE Consumer_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, Sequences\n\nCONSTANT MaxLen\n\n(* --algorithm Consumer\nvariables received = << >>, runningSum = 0;\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while Len(received) < MaxLen do\n      with v \\in 1..10 do\n        received := Append(received, v);\n        runningSum := runningSum + v;\n      end with;\n    end while;\n  Finish:\n    skip;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nBoundedReceived == UNION { [1..n -> 1..10] : n \\in 0..MaxLen }\n\nInv == /\\ received \\in BoundedReceived\n       /\\ runningSum \\in 0..(MaxLen*10)\n       /\\ pc \\in {"Loop", "Finish", "Done"}\n\nProperty == runningSum \\in 0..(MaxLen*10)\n====\n', 'abstraction_map': {'received': 'received', 'runningSum': 'runningSum'}, 'constants': {'values': {'MaxLen': [3]}}}]}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01R7xSQ5zu3RPQsytn4Ske4p', 'content': 'The bundle failed model checking. Details:\n\nTOOLCHAIN ERRORS (fix these FIRST — TLC cannot run until they\'re cleared):\n- refinement: SANY: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n\n- module Consumer :: consec: FAILED\n    violated_predicate: Inv\n    State 1 <Initial predicate>: runningSum=23, received=<< >>, pc="Loop"\n    State 2 <Loop line 29, col 9 to line 36, col 58 of module Consumer_Impl>: runningSum=31, received=<<8>>, pc="Loop"\n    raw TLC excerpt:\n      Computed 65536 initial states...\n      Finished computing initial states: 103323 distinct states generated at 2026-05-28 11:54:58.\n      Error: Invariant Inv is violated.\n      Error: The behavior up to this point is:\n      State 1: <Initial predicate>\n      /\\ runningSum = 23\n      /\\ received = << >>\n      /\\ pc = "Loop"\n      \n      State 2: <Loop line 29, col 9 to line 36, col 58 of module Consumer_Impl>\n      /\\ runningSum = 31\n      /\\ received = <<8>>\n      /\\ pc = "Loop"\n      \n      103957 states generated, 103339 distinct states found, 103151 states left on queue.\n- refinement obligation: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\nFirst error line: Parsing or semantic analysis failed.\n\nLast bundle slug: producer_consumer_system\nParent module: ProducerConsumerSystem\nModules: BoundedQueue(abs), BoundedQueue(impl), Producer(abs), Producer(impl), Consumer(abs), Consumer(impl)\nRevise the failing module(s) and/or abstraction map(s). Return one call to repair_module_bundle with the FULL revised bundle.'}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-7', 'system': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'You are repairing a multi-module ModuleBundle that failed one or more proof\nobligations under TLC. The user message lists each failing obligation: it\nmay be a per-impl (Init/Consec/Property) failure, or the cross-module\nrefinement obligation.\n\nYour task\n---------\nDiagnose the failures and emit a revised bundle via the\n`repair_module_bundle` tool. Set `targeted_failure` to point at the most\nimportant failure (e.g. `"Queue/consec"`, `"refinement"`, `"parent/property"`).\nProvide a brief `reasoning`.\n\nDiagnosis guidance\n------------------\n* Per-impl `init`/`consec`/`property` failures behave exactly like the\n  single-module flow: weaken or strengthen `Inv`, or fix the algorithm.\n* `refinement` failure: the impl\'s abstraction_map is wrong (e.g. it\n  projects onto a state that does NOT correspond to a valid Abs state) OR\n  the impl does something the Abs cannot simulate. Either fix the map or\n  restrict the impl.\n* Parent failures: the parent\'s composed `Inv` does not hold, or fails to\n  imply the parent\'s `Property`. Strengthen the composed `Inv`, possibly\n  pulling in an additional impl invariant via INSTANCE projection.\n\nOutput rules\n------------\nRe-emit the WHOLE bundle (parent + every module), even unchanged ones, so\nthe verifier can re-run cleanly. Do not respond with prose; call\n`repair_module_bundle` exactly once.\n', 'cache_control': {'type': 'ephemeral'}}], 'tool_choice': {'type': 'tool', 'name': 'repair_module_bundle'}, 'tools': [{'name': 'repair_module_bundle', 'description': "Emit a revised ModuleBundle after one or more proof obligations failed (a per-impl Init/Consec/Property, or the refinement obligation across all impls). Diagnose whether a specific module's Inv was too weak/strong, its PlusCal is wrong, its abstraction_map is wrong, or the parent's composed Inv/Property is wrong, and revise accordingly.", 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'required': ['reasoning', 'targeted_failure', 'slug', 'parent', 'modules'], 'properties': {'reasoning': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Brief diagnosis of which obligation failed and what changed.'}, 'targeted_failure': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Free-form pointer at the failure: a module name + obligation ('Queue/consec'), or 'refinement', or 'parent/property'."}, 'slug': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': '^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$'}, 'parent': {'type': 'object', 'required': ['name', 'tla_source'], 'properties': {'name': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$', 'description': 'Parent module name (matches plan.parent_name).'}, 'tla_source': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Full TLA+ module source for the parent: `---- MODULE <Name> ----` that EXTENDS / INSTANCEs each <Child>_Impl and defines composed Inv and Property. No PlusCal block here — composition lives purely at the TLA+ layer.'}, 'constants': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Finite domains for TLA+ CONSTANTS. Each key is a CONSTANT name; each value is a list of allowed values (small finite domains keep TLC tractable).', 'properties': {'values': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': ['string', 'integer']}, 'minItems': 1}}}, 'required': ['values']}, 'invariant_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Inv'}, 'property_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Property'}}}, 'modules': {'type': 'array', 'minItems': 2, 'maxItems': 8, 'items': {'type': 'object', 'required': ['name', 'role', 'tla_source'], 'properties': {'name': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$', 'description': 'Conceptual module name from the plan; final file names are <name>_Abs.tla / <name>_Impl.tla.'}, 'role': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['abs', 'impl'], 'description': "'abs' = abstract contract (pure TLA+ Spec / Inv). 'impl' = concrete implementation containing a PlusCal block."}, 'tla_source': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Full TLA+ module source: `---- MODULE <Name>_Abs ----` or `---- MODULE <Name>_Impl ----`. For impls, this must contain a `(* --algorithm <Name> ... *)` block; pcal.trans will rewrite the file in place. Do NOT pre-insert `\\* BEGIN TRANSLATION`.'}, 'pluscal_source': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'For impl modules only: same text as `tla_source`. The verifier uses presence of this field as a flag to call pcal.trans. Leave unset for abs modules.'}, 'constants': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Finite domains for TLA+ CONSTANTS. Each key is a CONSTANT name; each value is a list of allowed values (small finite domains keep TLC tractable).', 'properties': {'values': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': ['string', 'integer']}, 'minItems': 1}}}, 'required': ['values']}, 'abstraction_map': {'type': 'object', 'description': "For impl modules only: maps each variable of the sibling <Name>_Abs module to a TLA+ expression. Expressions MUST be in terms of the parent's own VARIABLES (the bare names declared in the parent module), NOT the '<Alias>!var' form. TLA+'s M!x accessor works only for defined operators of M, not for its variables — SANY/TLC reject '<Alias>!var' references with 'Unknown operator: var'. The parent's '<Alias> == INSTANCE <Name>_Impl WITH <impl_var> <- <parent_var>' has already bound impl variables to parent variables, and the refinement aux module EXTENDS the parent so those parent variables are in scope. Example: given Queue_Abs.queue and a parent variable 'buffer', write {'queue': 'buffer'}.", 'additionalProperties': {'type': 'string'}, 'default': {}}, 'invariant_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Inv'}, 'property_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Property'}}}}, 'notes': {'type': 'string', 'default': ''}}}}]}}
